# 低频词汇 List10
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List10核心词汇

notorious /nəʊˈtɔːriəs/ adj. 声名狼藉的 The area is notorious for crime. 该地区因犯罪而声名狼藉。
nurture /ˈnɜːtʃə(r)/ v./n. 养育 Schools should nurture students' creativity. 学校应该培养学生的创造力。
obsolete /ˈɒbsəliːt/ adj. 过时的 The technology has become obsolete. 这项技术已经过时了。
ominous /ˈɒmɪnəs/ adj. 不祥的 There were ominous signs of an economic downturn. 有经济衰退的不祥征兆。
onset /ˈɒnset/ n. 开始 The onset of winter brought cold temperatures. 冬天的开始带来了寒冷的温度。
oppress /əˈpres/ v. 压迫 The regime oppressed its citizens for decades. 该政权压迫其公民数十年。
orient /ˈɔːrient/ v. 使朝向 The program is oriented towards young professionals. 该项目面向年轻专业人士。
oscillate /ˈɒsɪleɪt/ v. 摆动；犹豫 Public opinion oscillates between hope and fear. 公众舆论在希望和恐惧之间摆动。
outbreak /ˈaʊtbreɪk/ n. 爆发 The outbreak of the disease caused widespread panic. 疾病的爆发引起了广泛的恐慌。
outcry /ˈaʊtkraɪ/ n. 强烈抗议 The decision provoked a public outcry. 这一决定引发了公众的强烈抗议。
outskirts /ˈaʊtskɜːts/ n. 郊区 They live on the outskirts of the city. 他们住在城市的郊区。
overhaul /ˌəʊvəˈhɔːl/ v./n. 大修 The education system needs a complete overhaul. 教育系统需要彻底改革。
overlap /ˌəʊvəˈlæp/ v./n. 重叠 The two responsibilities overlap significantly. 这两项职责有很大的重叠。
oversee /ˌəʊvəˈsiː/ v. 监管 A committee oversees the implementation of the policy. 一个委员会监管政策的实施。
overt /əʊˈvɜːt/ adj. 公开的 There was no overt hostility between them. 他们之间没有公开的敌意。
overthrow /ˌəʊvəˈθrəʊ/ v./n. 推翻 The revolution overthrew the monarchy. 革命推翻了君主制。
overwhelm /ˌəʊvəˈwelm/ v. 压倒 She was overwhelmed with emotion. 她被情感所淹没。
oxide /ˈɒksaɪd/ n. 氧化物 Iron oxide gives Mars its red color. 氧化铁使火星呈现红色。
pact /pækt/ n. 协定 The two countries signed a trade pact. 两国签署了一项贸易协定。
pandemic /pænˈdemɪk/ n./adj. 大流行病 The pandemic disrupted global supply chains. 大流行病扰乱了全球供应链。
paradox /ˈpærədɒks/ n. 悖论 It is a paradox that wealth does not guarantee happiness. 财富不能保证幸福是一个悖论。
paralyze /ˈpærəlaɪz/ v. 使瘫痪 The strike paralyzed the transportation system. 罢工使交通系统瘫痪了。
patent /ˈpætnt/ n./adj. 专利；显而易见的 The solution was patent to everyone. 解决方案对每个人都是显而易见的。
patron /ˈpeɪtrən/ n. 赞助人 The gallery relies on wealthy patrons. 画廊依赖富有的赞助人。
peculiar /pɪˈkjuːliə(r)/ adj. 奇怪的 There is something peculiar about this situation. 这种情况有些奇怪。
peer /pɪə(r)/ n./v. 同龄人；凝视 She is respected by her peers. 她受到同龄人的尊重。
penal /ˈpiːnl/ adj. 刑事的 The penal system needs reform. 刑事系统需要改革。
pending /ˈpendɪŋ/ adj./prep. 待定的；直到 The case is still pending. 案件仍在审理中。
peril /ˈperɪl/ n. 危险 The explorers faced many perils. 探险家们面临许多危险。
permeate /ˈpɜːmieɪt/ v. 渗透 Corruption has permeated every level of government. 腐败渗透到了政府的各个层面。
